@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Contact Role API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Account API Permissioning functionality in relation to Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Role" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Role  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Assign contact role to contact attempt
	Koroneiki contacts should not be able to be assigned to account contact roles on accounts by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry     | Automotive                               |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes        | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Sold By      | Liferay US                               |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I attempt to assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a non permissioned user	
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Default Account Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

Scenario: Assign contact role to contact via okta id attempt
	Koroneiki contacts should not be able to be assigned to account contact roles on accounts via contact okta id by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry     | Automotive                               |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes        | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Sold By      | Liferay US                               |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign contacts with the following okta IDs to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneikicontact1 |
	And I attempt to assign the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a non permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Default Account Role"
	And the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

